bolt3 — provenance note
=======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `bolt8`/`sphinx`/
`bip340`/`taproot`/`musig2` modules, which are likewise self-contained
crypto/codec modules not folded into the root `NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

bolt3 — clean-room implementation from the Lightning BOLT#3 specification
("Bitcoin Transaction and Script Formats", lightning/bolts), specifically the
"Key Derivation" section (per-commitment and revocation public/secret keys)
and Appendix D ("Per-commitment Secret Requirements"). Written from the spec
text and its normative test vectors; no reference implementation was copied.

The elliptic-curve group (secp256k1) and SHA-256 come from Zig's standard
library (`std.crypto.ecc.Secp256k1`, `std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256`). The
scalar-reduction idiom for hash-to-scalar mirrors this repository's own
`bip340` module.

Verification vectors are the BOLT#3 Appendix D (generation) and Appendix E
(key derivation) test vectors from the lightning/bolts repository, reproduced
byte-exact in the module's tests.
